# Patterns the push sidecar keeps out of its "agent WIP" commits. It reads them
# through core.excludesFile, so they apply to files git does not track yet, on top
# of the repository's own .gitignore. A file the agent already committed is not
# affected.
#
# Sources checked:
#   id_rsa*, id_ecdsa*, id_ed25519*  default private key names in ssh-keygen(1),
#                                    https://man.openbsd.org/ssh-keygen
#   .npmrc      can hold _authToken and _password,
#               https://docs.npmjs.com/cli/v10/configuring-npm/npmrc
#   .pypirc     holds usernames and PyPI tokens in plain text,
#               https://packaging.python.org/en/latest/specifications/pypirc/
#   .git-credentials  plain-text file of git-credential-store,
#               https://git-scm.com/docs/git-credential-store
#   auth.json   the file this image's Codex entrypoint writes the Codex login to
# Not backed by a document I fetched, kept as common practice: .env, .env.*,
# *.pem, *.key, *.p12, *.pfx, *credentials*, .netrc.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
id_rsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*credentials*
.npmrc
.pypirc
.netrc
.git-credentials
auth.json
